#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""beton — the invisible guard dog. One command blocks sites forever (MVP).

Principle: in normal life it does not exist. It kills only attacks on the block.
Safe MVP: everything is reversible via `beton revert-for-testing`.
Final irreversibility (verity+SecureBoot+key destruction) — Stage 2 only
via the --final-irreversible flag, locked in the MVP.

Simple usage:
  sudo ./beton                      # interactive: asks for sites, does everything itself
  sudo ./beton block youtube.com tiktok.com --yes-i-understand-this-is-forever
  ./beton dry-run youtube.com       # changes nothing, only shows the plan
  sudo ./beton status
  sudo ./beton enforce              # silently restore (called by the systemd timer)
  sudo ./beton revert-for-testing   # VM TESTS ONLY, removed in the final

Dependencies: Python stdlib only. System: Arch Linux, nftables, systemd.
"""
